speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, under Standing Order 43, I raise an urgent question to which, in my view, the House must give consideration.
Considering that the situation of a large number of Canadian farmers is deteriorating day by day and that Bill C-176 can bring some relief or even correct the situation; and considering that it is the responsibility of Parliament to act quickly with regard to this serious problem, I move, seconded by the hon. member for Frontenac (Mr. Corriveau);
That the House should instruct the Committee on Procedure and Organization to study the possibility of establishing a reasonable though limited delay for the adoption on third reading of Bill C-176, and to report to the House within 48 hours.
